; No LIBRARY statement on purpose. The output is ArchiveFldr.32.dll or
; ArchiveFldr.64.dll depending on the platform, so any name here would
; contradict the linker's own /OUT and earn LNK4070. The linker takes
; the name from /OUT regardless; LIBRARY only ever adds a way to be
; wrong.
; DllMain is NOT exported. The loader finds it through the PE entry
; point the linker already wrote; exporting it only publishes an entry
; point any process can call by name, out of order and off the loader's
; own sequence. Nothing in Windows looks it up here.
EXPORTS
    DllGetClassObject       PRIVATE
    DllCanUnloadNow         PRIVATE
    DllRegisterServer       PRIVATE
    DllUnregisterServer     PRIVATE
    DllInstall              PRIVATE